==English==

===Etymology===
As a surname ''Monelight'' in 1337, as ''Mone lith'' about 1300. Compound of  ''mone'' "[[moon]]" + ''lith'' "[[light]]".<ref>''Chambers Dictionary of Etymology'', Robert K. Barnhart (ed.), Chambers, 1988</ref>

